  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Civil Society in Swaziland</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1. Coordinated civic education conducted in collaboration with members, partners and consensus and propositions in certain areas.  
Outcome 2. National and International Advocacy that is informed by views collected through civic education
Outcome 3 A better co-ordinated and vibrant civic society with respect to issues of governance, human rights and participation.
Outcome 4 Monitoring and evaluation which informs projects and programs.

Activities
-Recruitment of Programme manager
-To coordinate the production of I.E.C material on Constitutionalism, human rights and governance in Swaziland;Production of 
brochures, posters,CD&#x2019;s and audio material: CD&#x2019;s and tapes
-Conduct country wide civic education, focusing on youth and women
- produce and disseminate, News Paper adverts Press statements, T.V programmes (phone in),Radio programmes
-Stage 18 performances of theatre on agreed civic education 

Indicators
-full time programme manager recruited for SCCCO
-activities of civil society showing evidence of coordination
-Number of people engaging on human rights, governance and constitutionalism from an informed perspective.
-Number of material produced;15 000 brochures per theme,1000 CD&#x2019;s, 2000 audio CD&#x2019;s, 500 tapes, Translation
-75 youth workshops, 60 women&#x2019;s workshops on human rights and civic awareness conducted.</narrative>
  </description>
